          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What kind of activity is described for someone with COPD who gets breathless walking?",
          "answer": "For someone with COPD who experiences breathlessness when walking, activity is very important to help prevent a deconditioning spiral. When breathlessness makes activity unpleasant, people tend to avoid it. This leads to muscles weakening, which in turn makes the same tasks demand more effort and causes breathlessness to occur sooner. The lungs themselves may not have changed, but the body using them has become less efficient.\n\nMuch of the improvement seen in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease comes from reversing this cycle through exercise. For this reason, exercise is considered a therapy rather than just general advice for people with COPD.\n\nThis information comes from the document \"Staying active with COPD: breathing technique, pacing and the deconditioning spiral.\"\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
